{"ts":"2026-08-10T10:19:41.258Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/terminal-write-refusal-retry-ownership.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["refused-terminal-keeps-retry-owner-and-arms-repair","drain-reports-truthful-progress"]}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"test-receipt","args":{"file":"solve/evidence/terminal-write-refusal-retry-ownership.receipt.json","requiredReceipts":["refused-terminal-keeps-retry-owner-and-arms-repair","drain-reports-truthful-progress"]}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"A refused terminal transition keeps a retry owner and becomes loud: OperationWorkflowTransitionPersistence.completeOperation/failOperation stop clearing terminal retry state at entry (clearing becomes a consequence of a proven committed terminal, never a precondition of attempting one), the committed:false REFUSED/REINSERTED/null dispositions arm the EXISTING operation-workflow-terminal-transition-repair (today reachable only from the afterCommit confirm path, leaving 'refused' — a strictly worse state than 'committed but invisible' — uncovered) with one typed warn, and completeOperation/failOperation return their typed transitionOutcome so the recovery drain stops reporting progressed:true unconditionally — giving the existing bounded-escalation family its missing terminalization-refused counter. Verified at HEAD d75b01706 across four red formation runs (ec-q6-20260810T09*): the coordinator decides to terminalize 175-249 times per run with ZERO 'Operation completed' lines and zero logging — completeOperation's first statement clearTerminalOperationRetryState kills the armed executor-outcome retry timer (silencing the visibility-deferral loop mid-backoff, timestamped to the ms), the terminal UPDATE returns disposition REFUSED silently via resolveZeroChangeOperationUpdate, and the drain returns true unconditionally after a void completeOperation so level-triggered machinery believes progress. Fail-closed floor: release-gated dispositions (TERMINAL_ADOPTED, IDEMPOTENT_REPLAY) keep today's behavior; no new timers (the repair's 0.5s-30s backoff exists); the raft-level root (stale-log leader election on replica_operations-p1) is explicitly OUT of this quest's scope and routed separately.","title":null,"class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."}],"verificationTemplates":["retry-loops","recovery-replay"],"frontierIds":["terminal-write-refusal-retry-ownership-main"]}}
{"ts":"2026-08-10T10:31:46.688Z","type":"finding","frontier":"terminal-write-refusal-retry-ownership-main","claim":"Election-safety research REFUTES the stale-log-leader premise (full report to be archived in this quest's change dir): base liferaft's 5.4.1 up-to-dateness check exists and is correct (index.js:228-239), the reconstructed term-2 election shows all three up-to-date replicas GRANTING (candidate equal-or-ahead; grants provable from raft.change leader side-effects since no vote logging exists), and the 68/70-style truncation refusals are benign-with-guard noise (base truncates on MATCHING prefixes, a 5.3 misimplementation; committedIndex climbs to 514). The live wedge root is a ROW-VISIBILITY gap at ownership transfer: new leader logs 'No row found for CDC update' for replace-op-b0b98821 8ms before driving it, terminal writes refuse (this quest's exact class), drain degenerates to fail_priority_recovery_drain_stale/evidence_unavailable. Follow-up candidates recorded, NOT quested yet: (1) transfer-time catch-up gate on requestElectionNow (Ongaro 3.10/etcd precedent — hardening, not this wedge's cause); (2) wrapper fix for base's non-conflict truncation (only truncate on term mismatch — removes 39-60 ERRORs/run); (3) vote-decision observability from the patched listener; (4) DT6 election tests run LOGLESS so 5.4.1 is never exercised — adding InMemoryLogAdapter to buildCluster is the highest-value test change. Prior art: research-lever-c-election-gap.md covers the inverse failure; CL-040/041/042 all closed and correct.","kind":null,"evidence":"subagent:election-root-research-20260810","rulesOut":null,"verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
